= Adafmt.com One-Page Site Brief

== Product Positioning

Adafmt™ is a modern, high-performance, safety-oriented Ada formatter for professional development teams. The command-line tool is `adafmt`.

== Core Message

Professional Ada formatting, built for real codebases.

Adafmt provides configuration-driven style correction, syntax error detection, automatic backup behavior, and repeatable formatting for standard Ada source code, including Ada 2022-oriented workflows.

== Visual Direction

Dark, cinematic developer-tool aesthetic with electric blue and green accents. Use a polished dashboard/workflow feel without centering the story on `adafmt.toml`.

== Site Sections

1. Hero: product introduction and trial-list call to action.
2. Proof strip: relevant ACATS tests, Ada 2022 feature coverage, 51,000+ Ada files in largest test corpus, real-world Ada corpus, safe by default, v1.0.0 Linux release planned.
3. Why Adafmt: less style noise, more engineering signal.
4. Features: modern Ada support, configuration-driven style, syntax error detection, safe by default, adaptive performance, CLI workflow.
5. How it Works: choose a style, run adafmt, review safely.
6. In the Lab: relevant ACATS Ada 2012 tests, supplemental Ada 2022 feature tests, real-world open-source Ada code, largest test corpus with more than 51,000 Ada files.
7. Performance: small, medium, and large benchmark results coming soon.
8. Migration: familiar concepts for GNAT Ada teams.
9. Release/trial: v1.0.0 planned for Linux amd64 and Linux arm64 by June 1, 2026; Windows 11 expected shortly afterwards; macOS supported with release packaging pending an external vendor library issue; 14-day trial planned after licensing is enabled, with subscription option at the end.
10. FAQ: search and AI-friendly structured answers.

== Claims to Avoid

- Do not claim compiler certification.
- Do not publish stale performance numbers.
- Do not publish ACATS percentages on the marketing page.
- Do not mention internal engine/project architecture.

== Trademark Rule

Use Adafmt™ on first prominent product use, Adafmt for later prose, and `adafmt` for command examples. Footer: Adafmt™ and adafmt™ are trademarks of A Bit of Help, Inc.
